{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473773-american-psycho-as-an-inspiration-for-vtm","id":1473773,"title":"American Psycho as an inspiration for VTM","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-01T13:59:41-08:00","id":1473773,"title":"American Psycho as an inspiration for VTM","content":"Do you think American Psycho works as a good inspiration for VTM? The general vibe of superficiality, vanity, and petty oneupmanship does seem very vampirey. And Bateman himself seems like he works as a Ventrue who is rapidly becoming a wight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T14:40:35-08:00","id":1473776,"title":"","content":"There's several non-vampire moves I use as partial inspiration for how I see Vampire. American Psycho is one of them. The petty jockeying between Bateman and his coworkers is how I see a lot of what happens in Elysium. The actual serial killer aspect, though, is not something I dwell upon too much.<br /> <br /> Other non-vampire movies that I use include The Godfather Trilogy, The Insider, Heathers, Metropolitan (by Whit Stillman), Elizabeth (Cate Blanchette), Usual Suspects, Margin Call, and Casablanca. All of them have something that I think can be used to reflect vampire society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T15:24:35-08:00","id":1473777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473773-american-psycho-as-an-inspiration-for-vtm#post1473773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think American Psycho works as a good inspiration for VTM? The general vibe of superficiality, vanity, and petty oneupmanship does seem very vampirey. And Bateman himself seems like he works as a Ventrue who is rapidly becoming a wight.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually did have a scene from American Psycho used in a game. The player characters find out a vampire they know has been dumping the bodies of mortals he's killed in an apartment. They're disgusted and ready to get show the evidence that he's a major Masquerade violator.<br /> <br /> Then they go back to the apartment and find the place has been completely cleaned and the bodies disposed of.<br /> <br /> The Prince having done it as a favor for the vampire they were hunting with a caveat, &quot;We have SERVICES for this sort of thing.&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T15:25:21-08:00","id":1473778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1473773-american-psycho-as-an-inspiration-for-vtm?p=1473776#post1473776\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Other non-vampire movies that I use include The Godfather Trilogy, The Insider, Heathers, Metropolitan (by Whit Stillman), Elizabeth (Cate Blanchette), Usual Suspects, Margin Call, and Casablanca. All of them have something that I think can be used to reflect vampire society.</div> </div> </div> </div>A good list. I'll add to it with Scarface, Ghost Dog: Way of the Samurai, Fight Club, The Third Man, Layer Cake, Baby Driver, Chinatown, LA Confidential, Training Day, John Wick, Spy Game, and Nightcrawler, as well as TV series like Deadwood and Breaking Bad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 02-01-2022, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-11T07:20:42-08:00","id":1474429,"title":"","content":"Mean Girls in the same vein as Heathers, Phantom of the Opera is good if you can tolerate Schumaker, Sweeny Todd for that 'just below the surface' feeling. Collateral for that 'endless night' feeling. Wall Street for that prospective Ventrue fledgling. Devil's Advocate, The Prophecy, The Secret Window and Ninth Gate are some good supernatural horrors that line up nicely with VtM themes. Ronin and HEAT are great for that feeling of supernormal people who have to operate below the radar of larger society, and they both have pretty great heist/action pieces worth borrowing from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27296-devidramoth","name":"Devidramoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27296_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}